# Intro
A single, fixed-mass star at the center of a uniform, periodic glass-IC gas
box, with photoelectric heating and LW/FUV Yukawa screened-diffusion
propagation on (photoionization and radiation pressure off). Checks the
converged radial profile of the propagated FUV/LW interstellar-radiation-
field energy density (`FUVSpecificEnergies`/`LWSpecificEnergies`) against
the analytic Yukawa Green's function screened-exponential fall-off, with
the screening length computed independently from the run's own
metallicity and density, via `isrf_yukawa_profile_check.py`.

## Metallicity
The Yukawa screening length comes from a dust opacity that this code scales
with metallicity relative to Grackle's solar value; at `Z=0` there is no
dust and nothing to screen, so `initial_metallicity` (env var, `run.sh`)
must stay above 0. It defaults to solar (`Z/Zsun=1`).

## Cooling
`run.sh` passes `--cooling` so `cooling_init()` resolves Grackle's
`chemistry_data` (including `local_dust_to_gas_ratio`, which the dust
opacity above depends on) even though gas thermodynamics play no role in
what this example measures. `GrackleCooling:disable_cooling_for_debugging:
1` in `params.yml` then skips the per-particle cooling/heating update
itself, so the gas's thermal and dynamical state stays fixed and the
propagated field is isolated from any gas response.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```
`--with-tracers=GEAR` is required: `FUVSpecificEnergies`/
`LWSpecificEnergies` live in `tracers_xpart_data`. The Grackle cooling
mode is not critical here (only `chemistry_data` needs resolving, not any
mode-gated species network).

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var -- gas density
(`gas_density`, atom/cm^3), gas particle mass (`gas_mass`, Msun), star mass
and type (`star_mass`, `star_type`), resolution level (`level`, N =
`(2**level)**3` gas particles), run duration and stepping (`time_end`,
`dt_max`, `delta_time`), metallicity (`initial_metallicity`), and thread
count (`n_threads`); see `run.sh` for the full list and defaults.
`run_name=<dir> ./run.sh` moves the run's outputs into `<dir>` once done, to
keep more than one run's outputs side by side.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_yukawa_profile_check.py
```
`run.sh` runs this automatically against its own `output.log` and final
snapshot. It bins gas particles by radius from the star, fits the semi-log
slope of `u(r)*r` for both bands, and compares the fitted screening length
against the analytic one (`--tol`, default relative error 0.3). Produces a
comparison plot (`--output`, default `isrf_yukawa_profile_check.png`).
